=begin
  bardanchor.lic -- anchor Traveler's Song (1020) to the inn you are standing in.
  A rewrite of Gibreficul's Anchor_1020.lic for Lich 5.

    ;bardanchor           anchor here
    ;bardanchor test      dry run: show the checks and the song, sing nothing
    ;bardanchor force     sing even if the room doesn't look like a bar, or you have head/nerve wounds
    ;bardanchor help      this text

  What changed from Anchor_1020:
    - Room name comes from the map / room title (checkroom is gone in Lich 5).
    - The town comes from the map; the LOCATION verb is only a fallback, with a 5 s timeout
      (the old hook could hang forever).
    - Pre-checks: Bard, knows 1020, enough mana, not stunned/dead/webbed, roundtime clear.
    - BAR-ROOM CHECK. Our own logs (Marchelle, 2026-10-14) show 1020 only took in the TAPROOM:
      Main Hall and Front Desk of the Solhaven Inn failed three times ("reflecting away from the
      ground"), the Taproom (5715) took on the first try. So stand at the bar.
    - Head and nerve wounds cut the success chance (-10 to -90, per the wiki), so it stops and
      tells you to get healed first.
    - Reads the real success/fail lines from our logs, waits out the sing roundtime, and puts your
      language back the way the old script did (speak common).

  Success chance (wiki, GM Estild): min(95, spellsong ranks x2 + 10 same realm + instrument
  + EMC/MMC + DIS bonus + d100) > 100. Playing an instrument helps.
=end

ARGS = (Script.current.vars[1..-1] || []).map(&:downcase)
TEST  = ARGS.include?('test')
FORCE = ARGS.include?('force')

if ARGS.include?('help')
  respond ";bardanchor        anchor 1020 to this inn"
  respond ";bardanchor test   dry run (no singing)"
  respond ";bardanchor force  skip the bar-room and wound checks"
  exit
end

SUCCESS_RX = /It enfolds around you gently like a giant's hand/
FAIL_RX    = /reflecting away from the ground like waves of water/
OTHER_RX   = /You can't|You are unable|too thirsty|You don't have enough|isn't prepared|You have no spell|Your voice|cannot sing/i
BAR_RX     = /taproom|\bbar\b|tavern|\bpub\b|saloon|alehouse|lounge|common room|barroom|bistro|drinking/i

def say(msg) = respond("[bardanchor] #{msg}")
def stop(msg)
  say(msg)
  exit
end

# ---- who can run this -------------------------------------------------------------
stop("Only bards can anchor Traveler's Song.") unless Char.prof == 'Bard'
stop("You don't know Traveler's Song (1020).") unless Spell[1020].known?
stop("You're dead.") if dead?
stop("You're stunned -- wait it out.") if stunned?
stop("You're webbed -- wait it out.") if webbed?
stop("Not enough mana for 1020.") unless TEST || Spell[1020].affordable?

# ---- where are we -----------------------------------------------------------------
title = (XMLData.room_title || '').gsub(/[\[\]]/, '').strip      # "Solhaven Inn, Taproom"
title = Array(Room.current&.title).first.to_s.gsub(/[\[\]]/, '').strip if title.empty?
stop("Couldn't read the room title.") if title.empty?

inn, nook = title.split(/,\s*/, 2)
nook ||= inn

town = Room.current&.location.to_s.strip
if town.empty? || town == 'false'
  waitrt?
  lines = Lich::Util.issue_command('location', /You carefully survey your surroundings/,
                                   timeout: 5, quiet: true, usexml: false) rescue []
  town = lines.join(' ')[/current location is (.*?) or somewhere close to it/, 1].to_s
end
town = 'this town' if town.empty?

say("Room: #{title}  (#{Room.current&.id || '?'})  |  Town: #{town}")

unless title =~ BAR_RX
  msg = "This doesn't look like the bar. 1020 took in the Solhaven TAPROOM, not the Main Hall or Front Desk."
  stop("#{msg} Walk to the bar room, or run ;bardanchor force.") unless FORCE || TEST
  say("#{msg} (continuing)")
end

hurt = [Wounds.head, Wounds.nsys, Scars.head, Scars.nsys].map(&:to_i).max rescue 0
if hurt > 0
  msg = "Head/nerve wound or scar (rank #{hurt}) lowers the success chance."
  stop("#{msg} Get healed first, or run ;bardanchor force.") unless FORCE || TEST
  say("#{msg} (continuing)")
end

# ---- the song: tell of the place, its surroundings and the objective -----------------
song = [
  "In the #{nook.downcase} of the #{inn}, here in #{town}, I make my hearth",
  "my objective is to return here safely with my companions whenever I sing of travel",
]

if TEST
  say("Dry run. Would sing:")
  song.each { |l| say("  #{l}") }
  exit
end

# ---- sing it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
waitrt?
waitcastrt?
before = checkprep
fput('release') unless before.nil? || before == 'None' || before == "Traveler's Song"

result = nil
begin
  fput 'speak bard'
  unless checkprep == "Traveler's Song"
    r = dothistimeout('prep 1020', 5, /Your spellsong is ready|You change your tune|already|can't|cannot/i)
    stop("Couldn't prepare 1020: #{r || 'no response'}") unless r =~ /ready|change your tune|already/i
  end
  result = dothistimeout("sing #{song.join(';')}", 8, Regexp.union(SUCCESS_RX, FAIL_RX, OTHER_RX))
  waitrt?
ensure
  fput 'speak common'
end

case result
when SUCCESS_RX then say("***** Anchored to #{title}. *****")
when FAIL_RX    then say("Didn't take (mana reflected away). Make sure you're in the bar room and try again.")
when nil        then say("No success or fail message seen. Check the game window.")
else                 say("Game said: #{result}")
end
